{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/766162-looking-for-sumerian-suggestions","id":766162,"title":"Looking for Sumerian Suggestions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-15T03:49:50-08:00","id":766162,"title":"Looking for Sumerian Suggestions","content":"Starting a Scion LARp, and one of my players wants to be a Scion of Ninurta. Just so I'm not reinventing the wheel, has anyone statted out the Sumerian/Akkadian pantheon? She wants to have Sharur as her primary relic; seems simple enough- big mace (Sun, War, maybe Justice). But Sharur was also intelligent and could turn into a winged lion, so also a Guide or a Creature... Any help or constructive suggestions would welcome, and thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7421-celtibear","name":"CeltiBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T17:55:55-08:00","id":767481,"title":"","content":"They have some fan-writeups of the Annuna-ki elsewhere on this forum, there's like 3 versions of them.<br /> <br /> You're running a Scion LARP? ...How? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T18:05:27-08:00","id":767485,"title":"","content":"I have a link to Gotham By Night's version of the Pantheon, if you want me to shoot it to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T15:34:09-08:00","id":768143,"title":"","content":"The same Birthright can be a Relic, Guide and Creature all at once. Though, obviously, while using it as a Creature, it can't be used as a weapon... so, some issues there.<br /> <br /> Cuneiform tablets, cylinder seals, beard ornaments, headdresses and weapons are all big parts of Sumerian culture. Pomegranates were fairly symbolic for them, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T05:32:23-08:00","id":769148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/766162-looking-for-sumerian-suggestions?p=767481#post767481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have some fan-writeups of the Annuna-ki elsewhere on this forum, there's like 3 versions of them.<br /> <br /> You're running a Scion LARP? ...How? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of mentions of the Annuna on the forums, not write-ups that I could find. Gotham By Night, the source cited everywhere in the forums, is no more.<br /> <br /> As for the LARp, a friend of mine adapted Aberrant to LARping a few years ago, and learning from his successes and mistakes, it's pretty easy. Moreso because even though Scion 2 isn't out yet, the damage scaling rules preview make LARping a whole lot easier, at least in theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7421-celtibear","name":"CeltiBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T05:36:23-08:00","id":769150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/766162-looking-for-sumerian-suggestions?p=768143#post768143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same Birthright can be a Relic, Guide and Creature all at once. Though, obviously, while using it as a Creature, it can't be used as a weapon... so, some issues there.<br /> <br /> Cuneiform tablets, cylinder seals, beard ornaments, headdresses and weapons are all big parts of Sumerian culture. Pomegranates were fairly symbolic for them, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking having her pay the equivalent of the costs of both a similar relic and a similar creature, and bump it up one point for the ability to shift between forms. I'll run the other things by her, too; thanks for the info! Mediterranean mythology is one of my weaker subjects- I always tended to Northern and Western Europe and Asia...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7421-celtibear","name":"CeltiBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T05:37:13-08:00","id":769151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/766162-looking-for-sumerian-suggestions?p=767485#post767485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a link to Gotham By Night's version of the Pantheon, if you want me to shoot it to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it still exist somewhere, as an archive? Even the Wayback Machine couldn't get me there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7421-celtibear","name":"CeltiBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T06:29:36-08:00","id":769182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltiBear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/766162-looking-for-sumerian-suggestions?p=769151#post769151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does it still exist somewhere, as an archive? Even the Wayback Machine couldn't get me there.</div> </div> </div> </div> Last I checked, it existed as a Dropbox. I'll PM you a link. Just to be clear, they've asked that it only be shared privately, not posted where anyone can get it. Not sure why, but there you go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T07:47:01-08:00","id":769235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/766162-looking-for-sumerian-suggestions?p=769182#post769182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Last I checked, it existed as a Dropbox. I'll PM you a link. Just to be clear, they've asked that it only be shared privately, not posted where anyone can get it. Not sure why, but there you go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woot! Thank you very much. This is a huge help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7421-celtibear","name":"CeltiBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T09:18:48-08:00","id":770777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/766162-looking-for-sumerian-suggestions?p=769182#post769182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Last I checked, it existed as a Dropbox. I'll PM you a link. Just to be clear, they've asked that it only be shared privately, not posted where anyone can get it. Not sure why, but there you go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it has something to do with them doing a similar game to scion. Here on the forums it was mentioned that (seemingly they said that) them still doing the gotham by night could have create some law wise problems because of their own game. Never got that though as you running a fansite and you creating a game that has aside from flair nothing to do with the fansite shouldn't cause any problems law wise (then again I'm not a lawyer though)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T11:01:34-08:00","id":770840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/766162-looking-for-sumerian-suggestions?p=770777#post770777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it has something to do with them doing a similar game to scion. Here on the forums it was mentioned that (seemingly they said that) them still doing the gotham by night could have create some law wise problems because of their own game. Never got that though as you running a fansite and you creating a game that has aside from flair nothing to do with the fansite shouldn't cause any problems law wise (then again I'm not a lawyer though)</div> </div> </div> </div>It undermines their copywrite. It's all post hoc damage control and would be largely ineffectual. There are some things they COULD do that would work better, but that would be legal advice and they aren't my clients. So, a big no no. (I am a lawyer, or was one, once. I got better.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T11:05:23-08:00","id":770844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/766162-looking-for-sumerian-suggestions?p=768143#post768143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same Birthright can be a Relic, Guide and Creature all at once. Though, obviously, while using it as a Creature, it can't be used as a weapon... so, some issues there.<br /> <br /> Cuneiform tablets, cylinder seals, beard ornaments, headdresses and weapons are all big parts of Sumerian culture. Pomegranates were fairly symbolic for them, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the nature of the myths, it seems likely that something could be a Relic, Guide, Creature or independent god all at the same time. Causality and consistency was not really much of a principle overall. In fact, redundancy was more important. <br /> <br /> Also, the &quot;mu-li-la&quot; (fertilizing pine cones) the &quot;djinni&quot; (winged men) are using to on the Tree of Life in oh so many friezes. Also the buckets holding, apparently, some kind of pollen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}